)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Job Data Set Panel                       !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  The Job Data Set panel lists the output data sets of one job: ? in the
}  NP column of a job on ST, DA, I, O or H shows it. INPUT ON adds the
}  job's input: its JCL as JES2 converted it and its instream data.
}
{  DDNAME   }The data set's DD name; JESMSGLG, JESJCL and JESYSMSG are
}            JES2's.
{  STEP-NAME, PROC-STEP }The step that wrote it; JES2 for JES2's.
{  DSID     }The data set's number within the job.
{  C        }Its output class.
{  REC-CNT  }Its records.
{  CC       }The copies to print.
{  CREATE-DATE-TIME  }The date of the job, yy.ddd.
{  FORMS, FCB, UCS, FLASH, BURST, PRMODE }How it is printed.
}  PF11 and PF10 move the fields right of DDNAME.
}
}  Action character:
{   S  }Browse the data set (Output Data Set panel).
}
}  END goes back to the list. The commands of the list panels work here.
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: contents   PF10: back   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHLSM
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
